<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.3.2: Using Completing the Square to Solve Equations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02369</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.3.2: Using Completing the Square to Solve Equations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>01fef4b0-22b6-4774-a366-8df757de2703</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><para id="para-00001"><term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00001">Completing the square</term> can be used to solve quadratic equations.</para>
<para id="para-00002">Example: Solve \(x^2+8x-2=0\).</para>
<para id="para-00003">To complete the square to solve an equation, follow these steps:</para>
<para id="para-00004"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Write the equation in the form \(ax^2+bx=c\).
  \(x^2+8x=-2\)</para>
<para id="para-00005"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Complete the square by finding \((\frac{b}{2})^2\).
  \((\frac{b}{2})^2=(\frac{8}{2})^2=16\)</para>
<para id="para-00006"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Add the value to both sides of the equation.
  \(x^2+8x+16=-2+16\)</para>
<para id="para-00007"><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - Factor the <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00002">perfect square</term> trinomial and simplify the constants.
  \((x+4)^2=14\)</para>
<para id="para-00008"><emphasis>Step 5</emphasis> - Take the square root of each side (remember the plus-minus sign with the constant).
  \(\sqrt{(x+4)^2}=\sqrt{14}\)
  \(x+4= \pm \sqrt{14}\)</para>
<para id="para-00009"><emphasis>Step 6</emphasis> - Write two separate equations and solve each.
  \(x + 4 = \sqrt{14}\)  or  \(x + 4 =\; - \;\sqrt{14}\)
  \(x = -4 + \sqrt{14}\)  or  \(x =\; -\;4\; –\; \sqrt{14}\)</para>
<para id="para-00010">Solve each equation by completing the square. In part a, select the value of \((\frac{b}{2})^2\) that will complete the square. In part b, choose the<emphasis>two</emphasis> roots.</para>
<section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00002"><title>Activity</title><exercise id="_008d3d4f-b998-4f27-83f7-aca8328cfb6b" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00001"><para id="para-00011">Enter the value:</para><para id="para-00012">\((x−3)(x+1)=5\)</para>
      <para id="para-00013">What is the correct value of \((\frac{b}{2})^2\) that will complete the square?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00001"><para id="para-00014">Correct! \((\frac{b}{2})^2 = 1\)</para><para id="para-00015">The correct answer is \((\frac{b}{2})^2 = 1\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_79029430-6d86-490c-a7d2-3acf7a23fa03" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00002"><para id="para-00016"><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> roots that solve the quadratic equation.</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00002"><para id="para-00017">Correct! \(x = -2\), \(x = 4\)</para><para id="para-00018">The correct answers are: \(x = -2\), \(x = 4\).</para></solution></exercise></section><!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->

<!--Q#2a-->
<example id="exam-00001"><exercise>
  <problem id="prob-00003">
    
    <para id="para-00019">\(x^2+\frac{1}{2}x=\frac{3}{16}\)</para>
    <para id="para-00020">What is the correct value of \((\frac{b}{2})^2\) that will complete the square?</para>
    <para id="para-00021">Write down your answer, then select the<emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00003">
<para id="para-00022">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00023">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00024">\((\frac{b}{2})^2= \frac{1}{16}\)</para>



</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->

<!--Interaction End -->

<section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00003"><exercise id="_76c1f248-4edb-4a02-9d24-dab54110bcd7" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00004"><para id="para-00025"><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> roots that solve the quadratic equation.</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00004"><para id="para-00026">Correct! \(x=\frac14\), \(x=-\frac34\)</para><para id="para-00027">The correct answers are: \(x=\frac14\), \(x=-\frac34\).</para></solution></exercise></section><!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->


<!--Q#3a-->
<example id="exam-00002"><exercise>
  <problem id="prob-00005">
    
    <para id="para-00028">\(x^2+3x+\frac{8}{4}=0\)</para>
    <para id="para-00029">What is the correct value of \((\frac{b}{2})^2\) that will complete the square?</para>
    <para id="para-00030">Write down your answer, then select the<emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00005">
<para id="para-00031">Compare your answer:</para>
   
   <para id="para-00032">\((\frac{b}{2})^2= \frac94\)</para>



</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->

<!--Interaction End -->

<section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00004"><exercise id="d20a0059-beb2-4112-8fb1-4ccc23cc7f14" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00006"><para id="para-00033"><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> roots that solve the quadratic equation.</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00006"><para id="para-00034">Correct! \(x = -2\), \(x = -1\)</para><para id="para-00035">The correct answers are: \(x = -2\), \(x = -1\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_4bac0056-6a2a-4f4a-ae8f-753e654ff4ae" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00007"><para id="para-00036"/><para id="para-00037">\((7−x)(3−x)+3=0\)</para>
      <para id="para-00038">What is the correct value of \((\frac{b}{2})^2\) that will complete the square?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00007"><para id="para-00039">Correct! \((\frac{b}{2})^2= 25\)</para><para id="para-00040">The correct answer is \((\frac{b}{2})^2= 25\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="abf2d852-e418-46c5-85cb-845a6773c2b7" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00008"><para id="para-00041"><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> roots that solve the quadratic equation.</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00008"><para id="para-00042">Correct! \(x = 6\), \(x = 4\)</para><para id="para-00043">The correct answers are: \(x = 6\), \(x = 4\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="e8b33f01-81e0-4dfc-910c-6fc0f6987a44" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00009"><para id="para-00044"/><para id="para-00045">\(x^2+1.6x+0.63=0\)</para>
      <para id="para-00046">What is the correct value of \((\frac{b}{2})^2\) that will complete the square?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00009"><para id="para-00047">Correct! \((\frac{b}{2})^2=0.64\)</para><para id="para-00048">The correct answer is \((\frac{b}{2})^2=0.64\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="c95204d9-28c9-4d83-a860-91c4b31263a6" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00010"><para id="para-00049"><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> roots that solve the quadratic equation.</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00010"><para id="para-00050">Correct! \(x = -0.7\), \(x = -0.9\)</para><para id="para-00051">The correct answers are: \(x = -0.7\), \(x = -0.9\).</para></solution></exercise></section>

